  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "So the obvious move is: just feed it more, right?",
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 2.679
    },
    {
      "text": "Show it whole buildings until it can imitate those too.",
      "start": 3.779,
      "end": 6.379
    },
    {
      "text": "Except that falls apart here, for two reasons.",
      "start": 6.819,
      "end": 9.139
    },
    {
      "text": "One the data simply isn't there.",
      "start": 9.699,
      "end": 11.579
    },
    {
      "text": "Imitation needs lots of examples, and in our world they barely exist.",
      "start": 12.079,
      "end": 15.779
    },
    {
      "text": "Every project has its own site, its own regulations, often its own construction system and its own client, so almost every real job is one where there's basically nothing to copy.",
      "start": 16.34,
      "end": 25.639
    },
    {
      "text": "Building-scale timber plans aren't just lying around on the internet.",
      "start": 26.18,
      "end": 28.959
    },
    {
      "text": "And two it's too much to swallow at once, especially when imitation is the only learning method you've got.",
      "start": 29.619,
      "end": 35.159
    },
    {
      "text": "Shape, scale, structure, quality, programme, all tangled together and just copying examples, the model can't get a handle on all of it in one go.",
      "start": 35.939,
      "end": 44.299
    }
  ]
}